{#
  BeMart admin login page — EC-CUBE doAdminLogin (管理者ログイン).

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 admin-theme `login.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/admin/login.twig).

  This is the top-level wave's login-context FORM page. It extends the
  admin LOGIN frame (`admin-login-base.html.twig`, the port of EC-CUBE's
  `login_frame.twig`) — NOT the standard `admin-base.html.twig` (which
  has the sidebar + header bar). EC-CUBE's login page likewise extends
  `@admin/login_frame.twig`. The markup skeleton + Bootstrap classes are
  kept verbatim from EC-CUBE; only the dynamic bindings are rebound.

  FORM-PAGE recipe (Ray.WebFormModule — see var/templates/README.md):
  the admin Login resource (src/Resource/Page/Admin/Login.php) exposes an
  {@see \MyVendor\BeMart\Form\AdminLoginForm} as `body['form']`. The
  inputs render through that real form object:

    {{ form.input('login_id')|raw }}    <- real <input> w/ id/attrs/value
    {{ form.input('password')|raw }}    <- real password <input>

  EC-CUBE renders the same inputs through the Symfony FormView
  (`form_widget(form.login_id)`); Ray.WebFormModule is BeMart's
  BEAR-idiomatic equivalent. `AdminLoginForm::init()` ports the field
  names / ids / attributes from EC-CUBE's `LoginType` (block prefix
  `admin_login`) + the template's per-widget `attr` overrides.

  VALIDATION AUTHORITY STAYS WITH the Be Framework Becoming chain — the
  form is a field-definition + renderer. On a domain rejection the admin
  Login resource exposes `body.message` and re-fills the form.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md, "Admin pages"):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}`  -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `path('admin_login')` -> deterministic `/{route}` (BeMartTwigExtension).
   - `csrf_token('authenticate')` -> EC-CUBE per-request CSRF widget.
     BeMart's CSRF is the CsrfTokenInterface (Slice 8); the hidden
     `_csrf_token` input is kept (structure) with the body's `csrfToken`
     (null in the html context — the EventListener mirrors the live token
     in). EC-CUBE-runtime only — enumerated as residual.
   - `error.messageKey|trans(...)` -> EC-CUBE's Symfony auth-error
     object. BeMart surfaces the domain rejection through `body.message`,
     rendered in the same `text-danger` block.
   - `"now"|date("Y")` in the copyright line -> the current year; the
     port inlines the EC-CUBE-equivalent literal.
#}
{% extends 'admin-login-base.html.twig' %}

{% set title = 'ログイン' %}

{% block main %}

    <div class="container" style="margin-top: 150px;">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-12 col-md-6 offset-md-3 col-lg-4 offset-lg-4">
                <div class="text-center p-5 bg-white">
                    <form name="form1" id="form1" method="post" action="{{ url('admin_login') }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken|default('') }}">
                        <p><img src="{{ asset('assets/img/logo2.png', 'admin') }}" width="106"></p>
                        <div class="mb-3">
                            {{ form.input('login_id')|raw }}
                        </div>
                        <div class="mb-3">
                            {{ form.input('password')|raw }}
                        </div>
                        {% if message is defined and message %}
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <span class="text-danger">{{ message }}</span>
                            </div>
                        {% endif %}
                        <div class="d-grid gap-2">
                            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-100">ログイン</button>
                        </div>
                    </form>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12">
                <p class="text-center mt-3">
                    <small>Copyright &copy; 2000-2026 EC-CUBE CO.,LTD. All Rights Reserved.</small>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

{% endblock %}
